This R project contains the primary code and data used for dataset production/assembly,  figures/tables, and analyses for the project entitled:\
\

\f1\b \'93Vegetation phenology and climate extremes\'94
\f0\b0 \
\
Below are brief descriptions of the data and code. Specific commenting in the R scripts throughout the R project provided detailed information on each step of the workflow.\
\

\f1\b \ul Code information:
\f0\b0 \ulnone \
\

\f1\b 00_get_data.R: 
\f0\b0 This script extracts, summarizes, formats, and saves the majority of the data used for analysis and figure production. This is achieved through a mixed of customized functions drawn from the \'91Functions.R\'92 script and existing R packages (phenocamr, MODISTools, and daymetr) that contain functions to download data. Processed data are then saved to various folder for figure production. Note that data in the \'91ngp\'92 folder were created in another ongoing project.\
\

\f1\b 01_create_figures.R: 
\f0\b0 This scripts contains all the code needed to generate and save plots in figures 1 and 3, using the data generated by the \'9200_get_data.R\'92 script. Note that each plot in figure 3 was generated/saved separately and then put together using adobe illustrator. \
\

\f1\b Functions.R: 
\f0\b0 This script contains customized functions primarily for accessing, assembling, and wrangling data within the 00_get_data.R script. The `get_daymet()` function is used for downloading and formatting gridded meteorological data from Daymet. The `sites_filtered_function()` is used to aid in selecting specific Phenocam sites according to specific criteria. The `create_raster()` function aids in turning a large tabular dataset of the northern great plains into a raster stack.\
\

\f1\b \ul Data information:
\f0\b0 \ulnone \
\
The data folder contains multiple folders, which are generally either contain single-site or multi-site data. \
\
-
\f1\b Site-scale data
\f0\b0  (specific coordinates) are found in folders \'91ap\'92 and \'91sgs\'92. These two folders are derived from the same workflow and contain MODIS-based GPP and NPP data and Daymet-based meteorological data for specific coordinates. These data underlie the plots in figure 1b,c in the manuscript. An exception is the \'91cperagm_GR_1000_1day.csv\'92 dataset in the \'91phenocam\'92 folder, which contains greenness data for a single location (the same location as for the \'91sgs\'92 data).\
\
-
\f1\b Multi-site data
\f0\b0  are found in the \'91phenocam\'92 and \'91ngp\'92 folders. The \'91phenocam\'92 folder contains daily greenness chromatic coordinate (GCC) data for select deciduous broadleaf or grassland sites in North America. The \'91ngp\'92 folder contains large datasets (eventually converted into a raster; ngp_raster_stack.tif) for the entire Northern Great Plains Ecoregion of North America. These data were generated from another project, and contain summaries of GPP (seasonal) and NPP (annual) anomalies (from their mean) during the most extreme (lowest annual precipitation) droughts in the MODIS record. These data can be viewed as a large-scale version of the data in \'91sgs\'92 and \'91ap\'92. \
}